<title>CANADA: Heavy snow and cold hamper railcar unloads - CWB.</title>
<headline>Heavy snow and cold hamper railcar unloads - CWB.</headline>
<dateline>WINNIPEG 1996-11-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Heavy snowfall and cold weather hampered the movement of railcars to export position in the week ended November 24, the Canadian Wheat Board said on Monday.</p>
<p>Unloadings at Vancouver totalled 2,590, below the 3,400 target. Prince Rupert saw a total of 1,158 railcars, down from the 1,500 target. Thunder Bay saw 2,689 railcars unload, down from the weekly target of 3,300.</p>
<p>Terminal elevators at the various ports made full use of their commercial drying facilities to dry grain harvested in wet weather, the CWB added.</p>
<p>-- Gilbert Le Gras 204 947 3548</p>
